The Canadian National Wrestling Alliance was formed in 1990 by businessman Frank Sisson and his partner Frank May. Located in Calgary, the promotion strives to keep wrestling alive in the once vibrant territory. Was one of the promotions to be featured on TSN after Stampede went out of business.
